# UI Philosophy

The application must feel:
- modern
- premium
- clean
- mobile-native
- smooth
- visually balanced

The UI should prioritize:
- clarity
- spacing
- hierarchy
- usability
- perceived performance

Avoid:
- cluttered interfaces
- outdated UI patterns
- inconsistent spacing
- overly complex layouts
- excessive visual noise

# Mobile-First Philosophy

This is a mobile-first application.

Every screen must:
- feel touch-friendly
- optimize thumb ergonomics
- minimize cognitive load
- prioritize readability
- remain responsive on smaller devices

# Design Principles

Always prioritize:
- simplicity
- consistency
- whitespace
- visual hierarchy
- intuitive interactions

Over:
- decoration
- complexity
- flashy visuals
- unnecessary animations

# Layout Standards

Prefer:
- clean layouts
- generous spacing
- predictable alignment
- clear content separation

Avoid:
- overcrowded screens
- deeply nested layouts
- excessive containers
- cramped sections

# Spacing System

Use consistent spacing.

Prefer:
- 4
- 8
- 12
- 16
- 20
- 24
- 32

Avoid random spacing values.

# Visual Hierarchy

The UI must clearly communicate:
- primary actions
- secondary actions
- important content
- navigation flow

Use:
- spacing
- typography
- sizing
- contrast

Instead of excessive decoration.

# Typography Standards

Typography should feel:
- modern
- readable
- clean
- balanced

Prefer:
- clear font hierarchy
- larger headings
- readable body text
- medium font weights

Avoid:
- tiny text
- excessive font sizes
- inconsistent typography scales

# Card Design

Cards should:
- feel lightweight
- have subtle separation
- maintain clean spacing
- use soft rounded corners

Prefer:
- subtle borders
- lightweight shadows
- smooth corners
- balanced padding

Avoid:
- heavy elevation
- aggressive borders
- noisy containers

# Button Standards

Buttons must:
- feel touch-friendly
- have strong hierarchy
- remain visually consistent
- communicate importance clearly

Primary actions should stand out immediately.

# Input Standards

Inputs should:
- feel modern
- remain lightweight
- use adequate spacing
- provide clear feedback

Avoid:
- dense form layouts
- tiny touch targets
- noisy validation states

# Color Philosophy

Prefer:
- neutral palettes
- accessible contrast
- limited accent colors
- semantic coloring

Avoid:
- oversaturated interfaces
- rainbow UIs
- inconsistent colors

# Dark Mode Standards

The app should support dark mode naturally.

Rules:
- maintain readability
- avoid pure black when unnecessary
- preserve hierarchy in dark mode
- use semantic colors consistently

# Styling Standards

Use the project's existing styling approach consistently.

Rules:
- keep styles readable
- prioritize reusable style patterns
- maintain visual consistency
- avoid duplicated styling logic
- prefer scalable and maintainable styling structures

Prefer:
- reusable layout primitives
- centralized spacing systems
- shared design tokens
- predictable styling conventions

Avoid:
- inconsistent inline styles
- duplicated style values
- giant style objects
- visual inconsistency across screens

# Reusable UI Components

Extract reusable primitives when repetition exists.

Examples:
- Button
- Input
- Card
- Avatar
- Badge
- EmptyState
- Loader
- BottomSheet
- Section

Avoid premature abstractions.

# Loading UX

Loading states should feel polished.

Prefer:
- skeleton loaders
- progressive rendering
- optimistic interactions

Avoid:
- blocking spinners everywhere
- blank loading screens

# Empty States

Empty states should:
- guide the user
- explain context
- suggest next actions
- remain visually clean

# Animation Standards

Animations should:
- feel subtle
- improve responsiveness
- enhance perceived performance

Avoid:
- excessive motion
- distracting transitions
- slow animations

# Navigation UX

Navigation should feel:
- intuitive
- lightweight
- predictable
- mobile-native

Avoid:
- confusing flows
- excessive nesting
- overloaded headers

# Lists and Feeds

Lists should:
- remain scannable
- have clear separation
- prioritize readability
- avoid visual overload

# Accessibility Standards

Always consider:
- readable contrast
- touch target sizes
- text readability
- accessible interactions

# Performance Philosophy

UI performance should prioritize:
- smooth scrolling
- fast interactions
- perceived responsiveness
- lightweight rendering

Avoid:
- unnecessary rerenders
- visually heavy layouts
- oversized assets

# MVP Philosophy

The UI should feel:
- polished
- modern
- reliable
- easy to use

Without introducing unnecessary complexity.

# Cursor AI Expectations

When generating UI:
- Create modern premium mobile interfaces
- Use clean spacing and hierarchy
- Prefer minimalistic layouts
- Respect mobile-first UX principles
- Generate reusable UI patterns
- Keep styling consistent
- Optimize for readability and usability